A||||5||88formula||Fiero Formula VS late 90'sHonda Prelude||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||03-17-2000||09:52 PM||||Was coming home from school late at night traveling down a two-lane road in my formula. A late model Honda prelude driving aggressively passed me going the same way. It was kind of “G’d” up with a large tine can muffler coming out the back and the passenger sitting so low in the car with his seat steeply reclined that I could only see the tip of his small greasy head. I couldn’t resist the temptation to challenge this guy to a street race, so I pulled up next to him at the next light and gave the twelve-year-old piece of Detroit iron a rev to let him know I wanted to race. When the light turned green he hit the throttle before I did beating me off the line (I was tired). I started to close the gap on him though when I ran out of rpm’s (I love torque). At six grand my engine sounded like a washing machine from the thirties filled with metal objects severely out of balance with no lubrication compared to his smooth go-cart-sounding engine that can rev higher than mine dose. When I reluctantly shifted to third he pulled another car on me (he has more HP). We raced to about 70mph and he never pulled more than a car length on me. Not bad for a stock twelve year old Fiero Formula.<BR>	The only modifications I have done to my fiero are an Accel coil and underdrive pulley from the Fiero Store. I have a borla exhaust with the chrome tips coming via UPS to me Monday and I plan on doing more go fast goodies in the future. I’ll keep you posted with pictures ASAP. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||03-18-2000||12:28 AM||||that's odd, i raced one and mine is auto,kicked his ass off the line had him buy a car length and still going but i had to stop cause a good old cop was at the next light.i guess when you do the heads and tranny and coolant and plugs wires cap and rotor they work great, hell i even beat a stang and a v6 s10 twice. maybe you should consider head work on your car cause my car rocks, and this is all stock motor.||||reg||14
Z||000002||AL||03-18-2000||12:30 AM||||forgot to mention 86gt.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||03-18-2000||11:11 AM||||Are your heads gasket matched and port polished? My engine is fully tuned up. I can’t beat a mustang in a race yet. A Honda prelude can reach 60mph in about 7 seconds. If a formula can get there in 7.5 than that sounds about right.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JIM GOOSE||03-20-2000||10:37 AM||||The other morning on way to office had a little dragrace with a 69-70 Olds Cutlass, might have been a 442, a little rough looking& making rumbly v8 noises. He and I were side by side up to 3rd gear for me which is a little longer shift. He pulled ahead bout half a car length and at this time must have been going 80, I let off. It was really fun and I think he was surprised how strong my car was, wait till I get the turbo setup going.||||reg||6
Z||000005||88formula||03-20-2000||08:32 PM||||I don't get it, how come my formula isn’t that strong. I've got 50k on my engine and it runs great. What the blank is going on here. My formula feels like a 140-hp car to me.||||reg||1
